the first test case, there are $$$13$$$ suitable numbers: $$$3, 7, 11, 15, 23, 27, 31, 43, 47, 63, 87, 91, 95$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of them can be represented as a sum of $$$3$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"zebra-like"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"2086E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2086/problem/E"}